From da6511dbfc6f3f28bca2d7e9e064eceab47f75ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Barth <dbarth4@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 13:14:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Drop the jiff dependency from rustc_driver_impl

jiff is pulled in for exactly one call site: naming an ICE dump file
`rustc-ice-<timestamp>-<pid>.txt`. That costs about 0.5 MB in
librustc_driver for a wall clock read and a six-field format.

Replace it with `SystemTime` and an inline days-to-civil-date conversion
(Howard Hinnant's `civil_from_days`).

This is not a behaviour change. rustc already depends on jiff with
`default-features = false, features = ["std"]`, which leaves `tz-system`
and every `tzdb-*` feature off, so `TimeZone::try_system()` always fails
and `Zoned::now()` already falls back to `Etc/Unknown` -- UTC. The
filenames rustc writes today are UTC and stay UTC.

Measured on a stage1 `librustc_driver` for aarch64-apple-darwin,
`strip -x`ed: 111,360,864 -> 110,857,848 bytes, -503,016.

For comparison, keeping jiff and only switching `Zoned::now()` to
`Timestamp::now()` saves 16,536 bytes, confirming the weight is the
crate rather than the timezone-aware type.

`portable-atomic-util` leaves PERMITTED_RUSTC_DEPENDENCIES with it; jiff
was its only path into the rustc dependency graph. jiff stays in
Cargo.lock because env_logger, outside that graph, still uses it.
